From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 00:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] DO NOT SUBMIT: arm64: dts: mediatek: add BPI-R4 Pro PCS diagnostics

Add four diagnostic wrappers for the BPI-R4 Pro 8X description. Each
wrapper changes only the MxL-facing AS21 at MDIO address 0x18 and MxL
port 13/channel 1. The combo-WAN PHY at address 0x1c and both SFP paths
continue to use the base board description unchanged.

The wrappers select USXGMII, 10GBase-R, 5GBase-R, or 2500Base-X and
opt the target AS21 into the verified firmware PCS diagnostics. The
USXGMII and 10GBase-R wrappers also enable the MxL flow-control
diagnostics used for their strict comparison. Fixed Base-R/Base-X modes
remove in-band management; USXGMII keeps it.

These temporary diagnostic descriptions were written by Codex.

Signed-off-by: Codex <codex@openai.com>
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt7988a-bananapi-bpi-r4-pro-8x-diag-usxgmii.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt7988a-bananapi-bpi-r4-pro-8x-diag-usxgmii.dts
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..75017163fd
--- /dev/null
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt7988a-bananapi-bpi-r4-pro-8x-diag-usxgmii.dts
@@ -0,0 +1,35 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0 OR MIT)
+
+/dts-v1/;
+
+#include "mt7988a-bananapi-bpi-r4-pro-8x.dts"
+
+/ {
+	model = "Bananapi BPI-R4 Pro 8X (AS21/MxL USXGMII diagnostic)";
+};
+
+&phy18 {
+	aeonsemi,dpc-pcs-diagnostic;
+};
+
+&switch16 {
+	maxlinear,flow-control-diagnostic;
+
+	ports {
+		port@13 {
+			phy-mode = "usxgmii";
+			phy-connection-type = "usxgmii";
+			managed = "in-band-status";
+		};
+	};
+
+	mux-bus {
+		ds-mux@13 {
+			channel@1 {
+				phy-mode = "usxgmii";
+				phy-connection-type = "usxgmii";
+				managed = "in-band-status";
+			};
+		};
+	};
+};
